  "aeroworks.ponder.console_configure.header": "Configuring Console Controls",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_configure.text_1": "Right-click while Sneaking to open its configuration",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_configure.text_2": "Key binds, Frequencies and other options are set per control",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_configure.text_3": "Held modules can be configured by right-clicking the air while Sneaking",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_control.header": "Controlling a Console",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_control.text_1": "Right-click with an empty hand to take control",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_control.text_2": "Keyboard and mouse inputs will move the mounted controls",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_control.text_3": "Each direction transmits on its own Redstone Link Frequency",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_control.text_4": "The transmitted power matches how far the control is moved",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_control.text_5": "Moving the opposite way transmits on the second Frequency",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_control.text_6": "Press [Esc] to release control",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_deck.header": "Console Decks",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_deck.text_1": "When several consoles touch...",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_deck.text_2": "...they can be controlled together",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_deck.text_3": "Consoles placed apart will remain separate stations",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_deck.text_4": "Only one player can control a deck at a time",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_heads.header": "Stacking Control Modules",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_heads.text_1": "Some modules provide a small socket of their own",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_heads.text_2": "Right-click it with a small module to attach a head",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_heads.text_3": "Heads will move together with the control beneath them",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_heads.text_4": "Their inputs work like any other control",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_mounting.header": "Mounting Controls on a Console",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_mounting.text_1": "Consoles provide sockets for mounting Control Modules",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_mounting.text_2": "Right-click a socket with a module to mount it",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_mounting.text_3": "Several modules can share the same console",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_mounting.text_4": "Smaller modules also fit into larger sockets",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_mounting.text_5": "Modules can be removed using a Wrench",
  "aeroworks.ponder.console_mounting.text_6": "They will keep their settings when removed",
  "aeroworks.ponder.mechanical_servo.header": "Controlling Rotational Angles using Mechanical Servos",
  "aeroworks.ponder.mechanical_servo.text_1": "Mechanical Servos relay a rotational angle based on the input redstone signal",
  "aeroworks.ponder.mechanical_servo.text_2": "Right-click to configure its rotation range",
  "aeroworks.ponder.mechanical_servo.text_3": "At full signal strength, the Servo rotates to the end of its range",
  "aeroworks.ponder.mechanical_servo.text_4": "The Servo rotates to an angle proportional to the signal strength",
  "aeroworks.ponder.mechanical_servo.text_5": "Before responding to a new signal, the Servo will finish its current rotation",
  "aeroworks.ponder.stepper_servo.header": "Controlling Rotational Angles using Stepper Servos",
  "aeroworks.ponder.stepper_servo.text_1": "Stepper Servos rotate to an angle proportional to the signal strength",
  "aeroworks.ponder.stepper_servo.text_2": "Right-click to set the angle of each step",
  "aeroworks.ponder.stepper_servo.text_3": "A stronger signal rotates the Stepper more",
  "aeroworks.ponder.stepper_servo.text_4": "Before responding to a new signal, the Stepper will finish its current rotation",
  "aeroworks.ponder.stepper_servo.text_5": "Only then will it move to the new target",
  "aeroworks.ponder.stepper_servo_dual.header": "Controlling the Stepper Servo Rotational Direction",
  "aeroworks.ponder.stepper_servo_dual.text_1": "A Stepper Servo accepts a signal from either side",
  "aeroworks.ponder.stepper_servo_dual.text_2": "A signal on one side rotates the Stepper one way",
  "aeroworks.ponder.stepper_servo_dual.text_3": "A signal on the other side rotates it the other way",
  "aeroworks.ponder.stepper_servo_dual.text_4": "With both sides powered, the Servo has no target and holds its position",
